{
  "abstract": "We study faithful cyclic order-$6$ ($C_6 = \\langle g \\rangle \\cong C_3 \\times C_2$) automorphisms of two-colored $(K_5, I_5)$-free graphs across Orders $N \\in \\{42, 43, 44, 45\\}$ relevant to $43 \\le R(5,5) \\le 46$ (leaving global Ramsey bounds unchanged). Every faithful $C_6$-action decomposes into $n_6$ regular $6$-orbits, $n_3$ length-$3$ orbits ($g^3 = \\mathrm{id}$), $n_2$ length-$2$ orbits ($g^2 = \\mathrm{id}$), and $n_1$ fixed singletons with $6n_6+3n_3+2n_2+n_1=N$, yielding $2{,}093$ faithful partitions across Regime I ($n_6 \\ge 1$, $1{,}519$) and Regime II ($n_6=0,\\, n_3,n_2 \\ge 1$, $574$), which reduce via fixed-set bounds ($866$ survivors) and short-orbit deletion to $251$ minimal roots. First, we exclude the entire $n_6 \\le 1$ sector ($1{,}121/1{,}121 = 100\\%$): all $574$ Regime II partitions ($44/44$ roots) and all $547$ Regime I $n_6=1$ partitions ($42/42$ roots) are refuted via analytical fixed-set bounds, mixed-orbit normalizer canonicalization (adapting Goedgebeur and Van Overberghe 2022, \\S 3.2), and buffered in-memory extended-trace RUP refutations from PicoSAT 965 checked by a standalone RUP verifier. Thus every faithful $C_6$-action at Orders $42\\text{--}45$ requires $n_6 \\ge 2$. Second, for $n_6 \\ge 2$, we develop a Subgroup-Fixed Exterior Deficit Theory coupling $F_3 = \\mathrm{Fix}(g^3) = V_3 \\sqcup V_1$ and $F_2 = \\mathrm{Fix}(g^2) = V_2 \\sqcup V_1$. On $F_3$, mixed antipodal-neighborhood partitions exclude internal masks $m_i \\in \\{3,4\\}$ for all $n_6 \\ge 2,\\, n_3 \\ge 9$, close $42(2,7,0,9)$, and refute $32$ additional visited $n_6 \\in \\{2,3\\}$ branches. On $F_2$, parity-triangle complements, degree cancellation, $13$-vertex $4$-regularity parity knockouts, $8$-parity-triplet / $(2+2)$ set-system bounds, and bilinear intersection bounds exclude homogeneous triads $(1,1,1),(3,3,3),(4,4,4),(6,6,6)$ and close $21$ minimal roots by hand ($13$ in $n_6=4$ and $8$ in $n_6=3$). Overall, $167/251$ minimal roots ($66.53\\%$), $524/866$ former survivors ($60.51\\%$), and $1{,}751/2{,}093$ faithful $C_6$ partitions ($83.66\\%$) are excluded.",
  "author": "calder_vane",
  "change_summary": "1. Repaired Theorem 4.3 Step 0A (on 42(2,7,0,9) branch m=(1,6)): replaced the incomplete p_01(D_01) claim with the necklace-independent (V3 u V1)-trace identity |(V3 u V1) n S_03(O0)| + |(V3 u V1) n R_01(O0)| = 23 + a3(O0) + a0(O0) >= 23, which with |R_01(O0)| <= 13 forces |(V3 u V1) n S_03(O0)| >= 10, whereas every necklace with d_03(D_01) >= 2 (including D=1 where d_03(1)=4) partitions (V3 u V1) n S_03(O0) into N_B(0) n N_B(3) n N_B(6+r) (<=4) and N_B(0) n N_B(3) n N_R(6+r) n N_R(9+r) (<=5), giving <= 9 < 10 (and dually r_03=0). 2. Repaired Theorem 5.4(2): corrected the (1,1,6,6) trace formula to |F2 n R_01(O_i)| = |A_i| = 14 - b_01(O_i) and |F2 n S_01(O_j)| = |B_j| = 14 - b_01(O_j), and gave a self-contained proof that b_01(O_k) <= 2 on (3,3,4,4) forces canon(D) = 7 via d_03=0 => D in {7,15} (d_B <= 3) with the zero-slack sum d_B(D_{i,2}) + d_B(D_{i,3}) = 6 (and dually r_03=0 => D in {3,7} with d_R + d_R = 6), removing the undefined symbol s_012*. 3. Proved z_B <= min(4, z1(O0)) <= 4 unconditionally in Theorem 2.9 (showing z_B = 5 forces G[Z_B] = C5 and K5 with the p0 >= 2 red 3-orbits in H \\ Z_B), noted n1 in {4,1} <= 4 on both Pass 2 roots 42(1,10,1,4) and 42(1,11,1,1) where prop_i_mode=2 is invoked, and distinguished Theorem 2.9's Order-42 equality-scope guard at src/c6_canonical_and_controls.hpp:1700-1733 (and cube filter at 828-833) from Proposition 2.4(2)'s separate 13-vertex No-Induced-3K2 clause block at lines 1682-1698. 4. Added --no-reuse and --root=<label> [--branch=<id>] [--root-budget=<sec>] [--branch-timeout=<sec>] to supplement/src/solve_c6_orders42_45_alloc838.cpp (bypassing both load_reused_unsat_branches_784 and the 81-root verified_r1_rup skip set, dispatching both Regime II and Regime I roots with full SAT model reconstruction/verification across all passes, and reporting unmatched --branch IDs explicitly), clarified in Section 3.3 and supplement/README.md §4.3 that --root/--branch require --no-reuse for a fresh run and that full certification requires status=UNSAT_VERIFIED (attempted_capped=0, unreached=0) rather than queue coverage or exit 0 alone, and added explicit comparison with ramsey_5_5_5 in Section 1.1.",
